--- body ---
## Complaint
Author, 2026-10-27: skills start with the same paragraph, "For helper commands, set `IDH_ROOT=…`". The checklist flags a skill restating what another owns; here 16 of 38 `skills/*/SKILL.md` carry the paragraph, 14 of them verbatim, about 326 bytes each (about 5 KB in all, loaded with each skill, not resident). Measured on origin/main 1b427518.

## What is already known (for the chart, not a diagnosis)
- The repetition is deliberate and enforced: the loaded-skill path seam (ticket 0803; `tests/test_skill_seam.py`, including `test_the_canonical_one_line_spelling_dominates`). Each runtime supplies only the loaded skill's own path, so each skill derives the helper root itself.
- yawn is the cross-runtime proof slice for the seam (`adapters/README.md`, `adapters/pilot-support.json`): any remedy is checked on Claude Code, Codex and Pi alike.

## The visit
Run `/harness-doctor` (the visit form from 1238) with this complaint. The doctor examines, gives a differential (e.g. necessary per-skill cost; a resident rule could carry it; a shorter canonical line; the runtime could supply the root; only skills that run helpers need it, and some carry it without using it), confirms with the cheapest observation, and offers priced options with odds, one recommended. The author decides; nothing changes before that.

## Exit criteria
- [x] One visit run, journal entry written in the harness's repository memory
- [x] Diagnosis with confidence, and what stays unexplained
- [x] Options priced (author-hours, agent cost) with odds and undo, one recommended, each checked against the seam tests and the three-runtime proof slice
- [x] The author's choice recorded here; a chosen remedy filed as its own ticket, or the duplication accepted with its reason in `skills/harness-doctor/references/checklist.md`

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)
- Premise check (recounted on this tree): the paragraph is not expired. 16 of 38
  skills open with "For helper commands, set `IDH_ROOT=...`": 14 verbatim (325
  bytes of text, 326 with newline), plus two shortened (hoard, 95 bytes;
  verify-gate, 207 bytes) = about 5 KB. Roar is a 17th spelling of the seam,
  two-step, not the paragraph. All 16 actually run a helper (`$IDH_ROOT` is used
  1 to 8 times in each; release, once), so "carries it without using it" is not
  borne out here; a hand-pruning option would target release/hoard-class single
  users at best. Seam tests: `test_every_seam_body_derives...` (floor 10) and
  `test_the_canonical_one_line_spelling_dominates` (floor 14, met exactly by the
  14 verbatim: any shortening or removal of one verbatim copy fails it).
- Running the visit in a hunt: executor loads `skills/harness-doctor/SKILL.md`
  and its references, runs the `harness_here.sh` gate, then a complaint-started
  visit (the ticket is the author's complaint; a hunt launched on it counts as
  called). Cheapest probes: recount (done above), lint with its positive control
  (`tests/fixtures/harness-doctor/trace-doctor-SKILL.md`), read
  `tests/test_skill_seam.py` and `adapters/README.md`; no model-spending probe, so
  no consent step. Runtime question per exit criterion: for each option, state
  what Claude Code, Codex and Pi would have to supply; where a runtime cannot be
  run, report "unavailable", not clean. It writes one journal entry,
  `memory/journal/2026/2026-10-27-harness-doctor-idh-root-paragraph-1240.md`
  (the existing doctor entries sit in `memory/journal/2026/`), with: diagnosis
  and confidence, what stays unexplained, hypotheses with odds, priced options
  (author-hours, agent cost, odds, undo, seam-test and three-runtime check), one
  recommendation. Done = the entry exists plus the first three exit criteria
  ticked; the fourth (author's choice) is not the executor's: leave it open and
  say so; the ticket then stays open (no close claim) until the author rules.
  The MR contains the journal entry and the ticket's ticked boxes/log only.
  Do not close the ticket in the MR.
- Antipattern scan: the risk is a doctor "fixing" the duplication on the spot
  (shortening the line, editing tests, adding a rule). Forbidden by the ticket
  ("nothing changes before the author decides"): the diff must touch no
  `skills/`, `rules/`, `tests/`, `scripts/`; the verifier checks by path. Also
  avoid a null-as-finding trap: "no better remedy" needs a positive control, and
  "nothing worth doing" is a legitimate priced option. Pre-weighed hint, not a
  decision: the seam tests encode the duplication as a safeguard, so accept-with-
  reason in `checklist.md` is likely cheap, but that edit also waits for the author.
- Shared-file note: 1237 and 1227/gaze (gaze, verify-adherence), 1239
  (test-doctor), 1246 (raid), 1244 (merge) edit skills that carry the paragraph.
  No conflict: this visit edits none of them. Risk is only the recount going
  stale if one of them touches the paragraph; the entry should quote the commit
  it measured. Run after those merge or accept a small recount drift. The
  uncommitted modification to ticket 1237 in the prep worktree is unrelated.
- Verdict: GO. Priced: executor about 1 agent-hour (read-only, one journal
  file), author about 0.25 h to rule.

## Raid feasibility (2026-10-27)
PASS. Recount holds (16 of 38 SKILL.md carry the paragraph). `harness_here.sh`, the lint fixture, both seam test names and the `memory/journal/2026/` doctor entries exist. The diff (journal entry plus ticket only) is bookkeeping tier (`memory/`, `tickets/*.erg`), so it needs no gaze and no full gate.
- Note: harness-doctor's stance says "Only the author starts a visit" and "Listen first". The raid launch is valid only because the ticket body is the author's complaint, so the entry should say so. The visit must not stop to ask the author anything: none of its probes spends model usage.
- No conflict with the other five tickets: 1237 (if retargeted to removal) deletes no seam-bearing skill.
